==English==

===Etymology===
From {{m|en|literate}} + {{m|en|-cy}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|en|/ˈlɪtəɹəsi/|/ˈlɪtɹəsi/}}
* {{a|GA}} {{IPA|en|/ˈlɪtəɹəsi/|[-ɾ(ə)ɹə-]|/ˈlɪtɹəsi/}}
* {{audio|en|En-us-literacy.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{hyphenation|en|li|ter|a|cy}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# The [[ability]] to [[read]] and [[write]].
# {{lb|en|by extension}} The ability to [[understand]] and [[evaluate]] something.
#: {{co|en|[[computer literacy|computer '''literacy''']]}}
#: {{co|en|media '''literacy'''}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Tory Shepherd|title=Can pornography be healthy? If it follows six rules, perhaps|work=The Guardian|date=2023-06-09|url=https://www.theguardian.com/lifeandstyle/2023/jun/10/can-pornography-be-healthy-if-it-follows-six-rules-perhaps|issn=0261-3077|passage=Prof Alan McKee, who led the project, argues that young adults should be taught “porn '''literacy'''” to help them “read porn well” and look for healthy and ethical depictions of sex.}}

